  "job_B1.6.4_20251001_193255": {
    "text": "\u00c6nig \u00feing wununge h\u00e6fde wyrcean.\nFur\u00f0or smea\u00f0 fandige God se bi\u00f0 \u00feam men \u00feonne hl\u00e6dre arer\u00f0 & astih\u00f0 \u00feonne uppan \u00fe\u00e6re\nOngan n\u00e6fre almihtiga f\u00e6der, ac he w\u00e6s sunu efre of him acennedde al swa mihtig swa he wes se of\nHalga heora begra lufe nes nefre ac w\u00e6s and \u00e6fre bi\u00f0 an God \u00e6fre wunigende on anre godcundnysse\nSwa hw\u00e6t swa lasse bi\u00f0 \u00feonne God \u00fe\u00e6t ne bi\u00f0 na God \u00fe\u00e6t \u00fe\u00e6t later bi\u00f0 \u00feone God \u00fe\u00e6t h\u00e6f\u00f0 angin na\nGod nef\u00f0 nan anginn ac \u00e6fre & wun\u00f0 a on ecnesse.\nSume gesceafta swa \u00feurh God habbe\u00f0 anginn endia\u00f0 & for\u00feam \u00f0e hi nabbe\u00f0.\nSyndon sume hwile.\n\u00de\u00e6t & fugelas.\nW\u00e6ron \u00feurh God & hi nohte.\nNu synd o\u00fere gesceafta gescapene \u00feurh God anginn & nabba\u00f0 n\u00e6nne ende syndon ece on \u00fean \u00e6ftram\n\u00de\u00e6t syndon englas & eac menna nafre \u00feeah \u00f0e hi \u00e6r ongunnon.\nNe m\u00e6g sawle \u00feeah \u00f0e se lichama swelte o\u00f0\u00fee he on w\u00e6tere wur\u00fee forb\u00e6rned nefre geendian.\nAc heo bi\u00f0 yfel beo god swa swa englas beo\u00f0 \u00e6fre \u00feurhwuniende on ece.\n\u00c6lmihtig scyppend \u00fee ealle \u00feing gesceop ane swa ece \u00fe\u00e6t he angin n\u00e6f\u00f0.\nAc hesylf is eg\u00f0er ordfruma & ende eallwealdend God.\nNe ondr\u00e6t he nenne for\u00fean \u00f0e nan o\u00f0er nis mihtigre \u00feonne he ne fur\u00fean him gelic.\nEfre he bi\u00f0 gefende his gefa \u00feam \u00f0e he wyl \u00feing ne wania\u00f0 ne he nanes ne behafa\u00f0.\nEfre he bi\u00f0 \u00e6lmihtig & efre he wyle wel.\nNele he n\u00e6fre nan ac he lufa\u00f0 so\u00f0lice \u00fea\u00f0e god weorc wyrce\u00f0 fordo\u00f0 \u00fee unleafulnysse.\nMycel is se f\u00e6der & mycel is his wisdom lufu.\nLocu \u00feu nu georne \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u swa swy\u00f0e ne dwelie \u00fe\u00e6t \u00feu gedon wylle sunu l\u00e6ssan \u00feonne his leofa f\u00e6der\nWylt \u00feu fur\u00feor embe \u00fe\u00e6t smeagan \u00feone sylf ne canst embe \u00fee sylfne so\u00f0lice smeagan?\nSege me nu so\u00f0lice, miht \u00f0u geseon \u00feinne hricg o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00feinne hneccan \u00feeah \u00f0u lokie underb\u00e6c o\u00f0\u00f0e \u00feine\n\u00d0u scealt gelyfan on \u00feone lifigendan God & na ofer \u00feine m\u00e6\u00f0e motian be him \u00fee l\u00e6s \u00f0e \u00feu dwelige\nGod \u00e6lmihtig gesceopp \u00e6rest on anginne heofen & eor\u00f0an.\nHer ge magon gehyran \u00fe\u00e6t heofen n\u00e6s na \u00e6r \u00e6r\u00f0am se \u00e6lmihtiga wyrhta hi geworhte on anginne &\nAc w\u00e6s \u00e6fre unbegunnen scyppend swa mihtiglice gemacode cr\u00e6ft.\nEnglas he geworhte on wundorlicre f\u00e6gernysse & on mycelre manega \u00feusenda ealle lichamlic lybbende\n& on weorod he gesceopp \u00fe\u00e6re scinendra engla se fyrmesta on \u00feam teo\u00f0an flat mid mycelre modinysse\nGod hine geworhte wundorlic \u00f0a sceolde he gif he wolde wur\u00f0ian his scyppend mid mycel\nAc he ne dyde na swa ac mid dyrstig modignysse cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t he wolde wyrcean his cyneseld bufan\n\u00dea forlet he \u00feone \u00e6lmihtigan \u00fee is eall so\u00f0f\u00e6stnyss & nolde habban his hlaforscipe ac wolde beon\n\u00dea n\u00e6fde he nane f\u00e6stnunge ac feoll sona adun mid eallum \u00feam englum \u00fee \u00e6t his r\u00e6de w\u00e6ron & hi\n& hi to \u00e6lcum yfele \u00e6lcne man tihta\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t hi manna sawla mid synnum fordon for \u00feam mycclum andan\nGod wolde \u00f0a gewyrcan mannan of eor\u00f0an \u00fe\u00e6t he geearnian sceolde mid his eadmodnysse and\nGod \u00fea gesta\u00f0olf\u00e6ste & gestrangode his englas \u00fea forleton \u00fe\u00e6t hi lybba\u00f0 nu \u00e6fre buton \u00e6lcere synne\n& hi hine wur\u00f0ia\u00f0 to worulde mid buton \u00e6lcum geswince a on ecnysse.\nGod \u00f0a geworhte of \u00f0\u00e6re mid his halgum handum mannan to his \u00e6nlicnysse & ableow on his liflicne\nGod sceop him naman Adam & of his anum ribbe worhte him gemacan w\u00e6s Eua ure ealra modor.\n& God hi \u00f0a gebletsode mid \u00feissere, wexa\u00f0 & beo\u00f0 gemenigfylde & gefylla\u00f0 \u00fea eor\u00f0an & habba\u00f0\nOn six dagum swa swa us secga\u00f0 bec \u00fea menigfealdan gesceafta gesewenlice & hesylf \u00fea gesceawade\n& hi w\u00e6ron \u00e6tg\u00e6dere gude.\n\u00d0a geendode God ealle his weorc on \u00f0am seofo\u00f0am d\u00e6ge & hine on \u00f0am seofo\u00f0am d\u00e6ge geswac his\nN\u00e6s he na werig \u00feeah \u00f0e hit swa awriten si ne he mid ealle ne geswac \u00fea gesceafta geedniwianne ac\n\u00c6lce geare by\u00f0 orf acenned & mennisce menn to mannum \u00f0e \u00fea God gewyrc\u00f0 swa swa he \u00fea \u00e6rran\nAc he ne gescyp\u00f0 nane buton \u00feam cildum anum & ealle \u00fea nytena nabba\u00f0 nane sawle.\n\u00c6lces mannes sawle \u00fee on his meder by\u00f0 acucod gescyp\u00f0 se \u00e6lmihtiga God.\nHe Adames dyde swa lange swa mancynn & \u00f0es middaneard wunia\u00f0 & nyten n\u00e6f\u00f0 nane sawle.\nSume men wendon \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0eos woruld w\u00e6re \u00e6fre \u00e6lcum anginne eall swa nu is heofen & eor\u00f0e & ealle\nAc to so\u00f0an \u00fe\u00e6t God.\nSceop & hi n\u00e6ron na gesceafta gyf hi gesceap hisylfe ac hi geworhte God.\n\u00c6lc \u00feing h\u00e6f\u00f0 angin \u00feurh God butan se ana scyppend \u00fee ealle \u00f0ing gesceop se n\u00e6f\u00f0 ordfruman ac\nN\u00e6s hit na f\u00e6rlic ge\u00feoht o\u00f0\u00f0e unforsceawod r\u00e6d God \u00feisne middaneard gesceop ac w\u00e6s \u00e6fre \u00e6t\nUre scyppend \u00fea\u00f0a he geworhte Adam \u00feone frumsceapenan man syngian wolde \u00feurh \u00f0\u00e6s deofles lare\nGod swylce hu hesylf smeade \u00f0a iu embe \u00fea bote hu he hit gebetan \u00f0urh his halgan gife \u00fe\u00e6t he\nSe man w\u00e6s he syngian ne \u00feorfte & he w\u00e6re ges\u00e6lig gif he na ne syngode & \u00e6fre gif he his Drihtne\n& gif he syngode he w\u00e6re & sy\u00f0\u00fean deadlic for \u00f0\u00e6re synne fremminge.\nGod hine ne na\u00f0re healfe ac lett hine habban his agenne cyre.\nN\u00e6s geworht mid nanre wohnysse ne mid nanum synnum gesceapen to men ne nane leahtras on his\nGod hi \u00f0a gebrohte binnon Paradisum \u00fe\u00e6t we on englisc Neorxnawang.\n\u00de\u00e6r w\u00e6s wynsum wunung & hi wunodon swa hale on lichaman & h\u00e6fdon ealles geweald ge heora\nGod cw\u00e6\u00f0 to Adame, ne et \u00f0u of \u00feam treowe.\nGif onbyrigst \u00feu bist sona deadlic.\nN\u00e6s na se dea\u00f0 \u00feurh Drihten sceapen ne on \u00f0am treowe aweaxen ac \u00f0eah \u00fe\u00e6t gif he tobr\u00e6ce \u00fe\u00e6t lytle\nOn \u00e6lemiddan Paradisum lignum uite gehaten, \u00fe\u00e6t is, lifes treow.\nAdam etan on ende \u00e6fter his gehyrsumnysse & habban \u00fe\u00e6t heofonlican wununge mid \u00feam halgum\n\u00d0a w\u00e6s \u00feam deofle awyrgedum mode \u00fe\u00e6t se man sceolde \u00fea myrh\u00f0e geearnian \u00fee his upahefednysse\nGod hi \u00f0a adr\u00e6fde fram \u00fe\u00e6re myrh\u00f0e to mycclum geswinceum & hi on yrm\u00f0e lif sy\u00f0\u00fean.\nHi mihton \u00fea sy\u00fe\u00fean seocnysse \u00ferowian & hi biton gn\u00e6ttas & eac swylce flean & o\u00f0re gehwylce\nHeora gecynd eac \u00fea w\u00e6s on costnungum gewylde to rihtre wissuncge.\n& seo galnyss weax unwilles on him \u00feeawas \u00fee he \u00e6r ne cu\u00f0e wunnon him \u00f0a on & on his cynne\n\u00de\u00e6r to eacan hi swuncon & on swate leofedon & mid earfo\u00f0 him \u00e6tes tiledon on mycelere\nSe \u00e6lmihtiga God \u00fea engla werod healdan \u00fea gatu \u00e6t \u00feam ingange into Paradysum & \u00feam bebead,\nHim w\u00e6re \u00fe\u00e6t he wurde \u00fea ece & eallum his ofspryncge on \u00f0\u00e6re yrm\u00f0e ealle sceoldon on ecnysse\n\u00d0a forwyrnde God \u00fe\u00e6s inganges to \u00feam lifes treowe \u00fe\u00e6t we lybban ne sceoldon earmingas swylce we\nWell us welwillenda God \u00fe\u00e6t he on o\u00f0re wisan ure yfel & his mildheortnysse \u00fe\u00e6t he swa mycel yfell\nHit s\u00e6g\u00f0 bec & on \u00feissere gesetnysse \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0\u00e6r w\u00e6s ligen swurd gelogod \u00e6t \u00feam \u00feam halgum englum\n& he of dea\u00f0\u00e6 aras on \u00feam \u00f0riddan d\u00e6ge swurd of \u00feam wege mid ealle \u00fe\u00e6t we in moton gan to \u00feam\n\u00deis is nu betere \u00fe\u00e6t we on blissum \u00feonne Adam \u00fea \u00e6te & leofode on ecnysse his cynne swa swa we\nNu \u00feing \u00feam dysegan dwollice leofa\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t him genoh well si on worulde gif he lybban mot \u00e6fre ac he\n\u00d0onne him hingra\u00f0 he ytt gr\u00e6delice eft \u00feonne him drinc\u00f0 gif he h\u00e6f\u00f0 \u00feonne him c\u00e6le\u00f0 he cep\u00f0 him\nNis \u00feis nu eall geswinc?\n& gyt swarran ealle ungelimp \u00fee on \u00feissum life becuma\u00f0 \u00fee man earfo\u00f0 ealle areccan.\nUton we for\u00f0i hogian her on \u00feissum life \u00fe\u00e6t we mid geornfulnysse gewilnian \u00e6fre \u00fe\u00e6s beteran lifes",
